// @check
// @error-at 10:4 unknown name `high` in match pattern — an arm is a literal, a `const` with a literal value, or the `_` wildcard
// A pattern that is an identifier OTHER than the `_` wildcard, naming neither a type nor a
// constant (D3271), covers nothing — the checker rejects it AT THE PATTERN. Silently
// skipping it either acted as a phantom wildcard (suppressing exhaustiveness for the whole
// match) or surfaced later as a misattributed "non-exhaustive match" pointing at the match head.
// The exhaustiveness check is suppressed for this match (the bad pattern is the
// root cause — no cascaded missing-member report for "b").
function f(x: "a" | "b") {
  match x {
    high => print(1)
    "a" => print(2)
  }
}
f("a")
